        "id": 1125653
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-10-14T08:11:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Again, that is really odd, you should not be poking around in devices other than the one passed into you, right?\n\nDo you have a link to the code that does all of this somewhere?  As it has to be released under the GPLv2 license, it must be online already, right?",
      "parentUuid": "b37cf6e2_95715da8",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 117,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 119,
        "endChar": 21
      },
      "revId": "594d62382526d50ec46d1b57e80f053e8be629e9",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c9019e79_a71280dc",
        "filename": "android/abi_gki_aarch64_mtk",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 119,
      "author": {
        "id": 1970801
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-10-14T09:14:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Sorry. The WWAN driver hasn\u0027t been online exactly. \n\nThe WWAN driver provides some exported interfaces to another driver(Say **Driver A**) to use the device object under **some_class** . \n\n**Driver A** doesn\u0027t know how to get the exact pointer of the device object at the beginning.\n\nHence we provide an API in the WWAN driver, where **Driver A** can input a pre-defined proprietary parameter to search the pointer of the exact device object.\n\nThat\u0027s why we wanted to iterate the devices under **some_class**.",
      "parentUuid": "652d43a5_ea433dfe",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 117,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 119,
        "endChar": 21
      },
      "revId": "594d62382526d50ec46d1b57e80f053e8be629e9",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4aafa9d5_96b050be",
        "filename": "android/abi_gki_aarch64_mtk",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 119,
      "author": {
        "id": 1125653
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-10-14T14:10:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Sorry, but that is not how the driver model works, please do not do that.\n\nDrivers should only control the devices that are given to them by the driver core, they should not be attempting to walk all devices and find others and then do things with them, that way only leads to race conditions and other major problems.\n\nPlease follow the proper structure of the driver core model.\n\nAgain, if you can point me to where your code is at, I will be glad to review it and help find a proper solution for it.  As the license requires it to be public, this should not be a problem, right?",
      "parentUuid": "c9019e79_a71280dc",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 117,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 119,
        "endChar": 21
      },
      "revId": "594d62382526d50ec46d1b57e80f053e8be629e9",
